# What each secret is and where it goes. Engine: repo-secrets (devbox
# docs/repo-secrets.md). One row per line:
#
#   target | source | mode | kind [| recipients]
#
#   env     a KEY=VALUE secret kept off disk; target and mode are `-`
#   render  target = a generated env file (gitignored), source = committed env
#           files and/or env .age files, merged in order
#
-  | secrets/terraform.env.age | - | env

# The devbox stats publisher's R2 write credential (tools/stats-publisher, `mise run stats:publish`):
# STATS_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / STATS_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY = S3 keys of token nomadware-io-site-stats-write.
-  | secrets/site-stats-publisher.env.age | - | env

# The marketing site's local env: committed dev config only (Cloudflare's Turnstile
# test keys). No Resend key in dev on purpose: the endpoint answers `unconfigured`.
# To test real delivery, put RESEND_API_KEY in apps/marketing/.env.local (yours, never shared).
apps/marketing/.env | infra/env/marketing.dev.env | 600 | render
